# PR #449 Review

## Summary

- PR body has no `Task: @task-ref` trailer, so there is no linked task/spec to fetch via `kspec task get`.
- `kspec item get @triage-cli-commands` confirms the target spec and inherited traits used for review.
- `kspec validate` reports schema/reference OK and no trait AC coverage warnings for this item (repo-wide alignment/completeness warnings still present).
- `pnpm vitest tests/triage-cli.test.ts --run` passes (37/37).

## Findings

1. MUST-FIX — `spec-gap` action does not create a spec-gap-tagged observation
- `src/cli/commands/triage.ts:132`
- AC `@triage-cli-commands ac-7` says the action should create an observation tagged `spec-gap`.
- Current implementation creates a generic observation with `type: "idea"` and no `spec-gap` marker. I verified the resulting `kynetic.meta.yaml` entry is `type: idea` with only the content text.
- This loses the semantic distinction required for downstream triage/spec-gap workflows.

2. MUST-FIX — `triage export` ignores global `--json` precedence
- `src/cli/commands/triage.ts:487`
- `kspec triage export --format context --json` still emits markdown context blocks because the command branches only on `options.format` and bypasses `output()`/JSON mode handling.

